{"step": "decide_type", "detail": "RCA explicitly states the root cause is the demo's deliberate, working-as-designed fault-injection path (productCatalogFailure flag gating GetProduct), not an accidental bug in checkProductFailure. That rules out any fix that disables/weakens the flag check itself (violates preserve-configurability). Investigated whether a legitimate, in-scope code_fix still exists: re-fetched src/product-catalog/main.go (GetProduct, lines 366-402) and confirmed the flag-triggered branch returns status.Error(codes.Internal, msg). Cross-checked grpc-go's codes/codes.go doc comments: Internal is documented as 'some invariant expected by underlying system has been broken... something is very broken' -- not accurate for a flag deliberately simulating a transient failure (per src/product-catalog/flags.json's own description). codes.Unavailable is grpc's documented code for exactly that transient case. Decided type: code_fix, scoped to reclassifying this one status code -- minimal, doesn't touch the fault-injection mechanism, corrects a real, independently-verifiable defect in error semantics."}
{"step": "also_investigated_and_ruled_out", "detail": "Considered whether the flag's targeting evaluation context (NewTargetlessEvaluationContext) was misconfigured relative to a fractional/targeting rule, which could explain the incident's blast radius spanning all 10 product IDs rather than one specific product. Traced flagd's fractional.go bucketing logic and go-sdk's flattenContext -- confirmed the live demo.flagd.json rule for productCatalogFailure uses a plain JSONLogic equality check against the 'product_id' attribute directly (not the OpenFeature targetingKey), so NewTargetlessEvaluationContext vs NewEvaluationContext makes no difference here; ruled out. Separately noticed upstream main's demo.flagd.json targeting rule has both if/else branches returning 'off' (a likely unrelated upstream typo), but this doesn't match the incident's observed live behavior (real failures did occur), implying the hackathon's deployed flagd config differs from upstream main -- out of scope (not the RCA's implicated file, and flagd's live config is the target system's runtime state, which this capability doesn't read-write/modify)."}
{"step": "read_caller_side", "detail": "Read src/frontend/gateways/rpc/ProductCatalog.gateway.ts -- confirmed no retry logic exists on the calling side today. Documented plainly in rationale.md and the PR body that this fix alone will not reduce blast radius until callers add retry-on-Unavailable; not silently claimed as solved."}
