{"incident":"incident-002","step":"draft_proposal_v1","text":"Scoped revert of loadGeneratorTraffic to shipped default 'on', offered two equivalent implementation options: (a) scoped OFREP/admin update to loadGeneratorTraffic only, or (b) reload/restart flagd instance from shipped demo.flagd.json wholesale. Explicitly said cartFailure/recommendationCacheFailure (also live-deviated from shipped defaults) were out of scope and would not be touched."}
{"incident":"incident-002","step":"second_opinion_round1","reviewer_agent":"ae8f3020c90b0fb1b (general-purpose, blind)","given":"proposed config change text + verified RCA facts only, not own rationale prose","verdict":"FLAGGED","reason":"Option (b) (reload/restart from shipped file) would reset all three live-deviated flags including the two the proposal said it was leaving alone -- internal inconsistency between stated scope and one of the two offered mechanisms. Also flagged as worth noting: three flags deviating simultaneously in the same sandbox is consistent with a deliberately-configured shared fault-injection state, not necessarily 3 independent accidents -- draft v1 didn't surface this."}
{"incident":"incident-002","step":"revision","action":"Dropped implementation option (b) entirely, kept only the scoped OFREP/admin update to loadGeneratorTraffic. Added explicit caveat: 3 simultaneously-deviated flags may reflect a deliberate shared fault-injection state serving other concurrent scenarios; proposal asserts confidence code isn't at fault and flag state is the mismatch, but not that flipping this flag alone is risk-free to other concurrent activity -- whoever executes it should confirm that first."}
